meta {
  name: Get Sales Breakdown (Producer)
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/analytics/sales/breakdown?range=last3Months&groupBy=producer
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  range: last3Months
  groupBy: producer
  ~segmentBy: policyType
  ~compare: true
  ~carriers: 
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{analyticsToken}}
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("rows add up to the summary — null rows included", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    const premium = body.rows.reduce((sum, row) => sum + row.metrics.premium, 0);
    const items = body.rows.reduce((sum, row) => sum + row.metrics.items, 0);
    expect(Math.round(premium * 100) / 100).to.equal(Number(bru.getVar("analyticsPremium")));
    expect(items).to.equal(Number(bru.getVar("analyticsItems")));
    expect(body.totals.premium).to.equal(Number(bru.getVar("analyticsPremium")));
  });

  test("each row has a label and a share", function () {
    for (const row of res.getBody().rows) {
      expect(row.label).to.be.a("string");
      expect(row).to.have.property("share");
    }
  });
}

docs {
  # GET /analytics/sales/breakdown — sales by any dimension

  - **Module:** `analytics`
  - **Permission:** `analytics:read` (Agency Owner via enabled modules, Branch Manager by template; grantable to anyone)
  - **Data scope:** sales use the dashboards' clamp — agency sees the agency, branch sees their branch, own sees their own sales. `branchId` narrows an **agency-scope** caller to one office; a branch- or own-scope caller may name only their own branch, and `BranchGuard` refuses any other with a `403`.

  ## Query (plus the filter — see Get Sales Summary)
  | Param | Notes |
  |---|---|
  | `groupBy` | `producer` (default) · `leadSource` · `policyType` · `carrier` · `branch` · `zip` · `csr` |
  | `segmentBy` | Optional second dimension (≠ `groupBy`): `policyType` · `carrier` · `leadSource` · `producer` · `branch`. `groupBy=producer&segmentBy=policyType` is the multi-line view |
  | `compare` | `true` adds each row's `previous` metrics and `change` (% for amounts, points for the closing ratio) |

  ## Rows
  One per key, **null keys included** ("Unassigned", "No source",
  "Unspecified", "Unknown carrier", "No ZIP"), so premium, items and policies
  always add up to `totals`. Sales and households are distinct counts: under a
  per-policy dimension (line, carrier) a bundle counts in each of its lines.
  Line and carrier split a sale's premium by policy; `B4tEH` and `Allstate`
  are one carrier row. ZIP is the household's property ZIP; CSR is the deal's
  CRM, else the household's.

  `metrics`: `premium`, `netPremium` (null per policy), `items`, `deals`,
  `policies`, `households`, `quotes`, `quotedPremium`, `closingPct`,
  `closingGap`. `unavailable` lists the metrics null in every row for this
  grouping (carrier has no quote side). `series` lists every segment in
  display order when `segmentBy` is set.

  ## Errors
  - `400` — unknown `groupBy`/`segmentBy`, `segmentBy` equal to `groupBy`, bad range.
  - `403` — as Get Sales Summary.
}
